                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "CNJkb",
                  "name": "why",
                  "fill": "$ink-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Switch = [data-theme='dark'] on <html> — one mechanism for the blog's ThemeToggle, Storybook's decorator and the differ's capture URL. Dark is deliberately its own personality: terminal lime (#80ee64) on green-tinted black — light stays blue editorial, so the theme pair can never be byte-identical (the sanity gate's dream). accent-subtle in dark is 14% lime alpha, not a solid. Raw scales reference → board 01 Color Palette.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
