                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "U2mEL",
                  "name": "why",
                  "fill": "$ink-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "A list keeps what a slab drops: ordinality, and the list semantics a screen reader announces as \"3 items\". It also reads as steps a reader performs rather than source to inspect, which is the manual's genre. The slab's one real advantage is fidelity — verbatim source, no rendering decisions — but CodeBlock highlights nothing on its own, so it needs shiki in a workspace whose dependency budget is one, and its unconditional tab stop would land on every scenario card.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
